WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.136
In Wu Zetian's time, the cruel official Lai Junchen specialized in interrogating prisoners, and his methods were extremely harsh.

00:00:08.486 --> 00:00:14.174
One day, Lai Junchen asked Zhou Xing how one could make a prisoner confess.

00:00:14.524 --> 00:00:20.572
Zhou Xing thought for a moment, then slowly offered his own idea.

00:00:20.922 --> 00:00:27.186
Zhou Xing said proudly: put the prisoner into a big urn and heat it, and he will surely confess.

00:00:27.536 --> 00:00:32.000
Lai Junchen said with a smile: then allow me to invite you into the urn.

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:37.606
Hearing this, Zhou Xing froze at once, unable to say a single word.

00:00:37.956 --> 00:00:44.220
Terrified and pale, Zhou Xing had no choice but to climb into the urn himself.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:51.098
Only then did he realize the method he had devised had trapped himself.

00:00:51.448 --> 00:00:58.144
From then on, 'invite you into the urn' has been used to describe giving someone a taste of their own medicine.

00:00:58.494 --> 00:01:03.054
This idiom reminds us never to use a cruel trick to harm others.

